{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795539839,"nonce":"arA3tCIZeZb9C6QkTXFYXr4nhiU=","title":"Code editor minimap: .minimap(true) has no effect and the minimap does not follow scroll or edits","message":"Reported on GitHub as project-blinc/Blinc issue 87. Confirmed in the code:\n\n- `CodeEditor::minimap(bool)` stored `config.minimap`, and nothing read it; the editor built only the gutter and the code area.\n- The minimap existed only as `code_minimap(state)`, a plain Div built once, so its slider and bars stayed where they were painted until the parent rebuilt.\n- `build_minimap` highlighted the whole text again on every build (`get_styled_content_readonly`), and its `line_height_px` argument was unused.\n- Nothing on the minimap scrolled the editor.\n\nFound while testing it: an editor without line numbers did not scroll at all. Its content row took its height from the gutter; the code area sits in a horizontal Scroll, which does not pass its height up, so with no gutter the content was as tall as the editor (physics content 300 for 200 lines in a 300 px editor; 3932 with line numbers).\n\nDesign: the editor itself is the vertical scroll container, so a minimap in its content would scroll with the text. The docked minimap is a fixed child at the content's right edge (fixed counter-translates the scroll), with a spacer so text stays clear of it. A canvas draws the bars and the slider at paint time from the editor's lines, highlight cache and scroll physics, so the slider follows scrolling and momentum without a rebuild. Colours come from `--blinc-code-minimap-line` and `--blinc-code-minimap-slider` through `stylesheet_color`, as the waveform does. Presses and drags in the minimap strip are handled by the editor's own mouse handlers, so they scroll instead of placing the caret. Lines thinner than a pixel share one-pixel bars. A canvas or fixed child keeps the editor's scroll container off scroll rows, as the caret canvas already does when the editor has focus.","files":null}]}